ten to the advice of Jeremiah was exiled from his place"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["איעצך" "לכה איעצך" "וכי איעצך לא תשמע אלי"]} {:kind :other, :note "Gezerah shavah: the shared rare word איעצך links Balaam's prophecy to Moses' prophecy."} {:kind :other, :note "Contrast: Moses heeded advice and stayed in his place; Zedekiah ignored advice and was exiled from his place."}], :frame {:text "Deuteronomy 34:10 states 'And there arose not a prophet again in Israel like Moses.' The Sages interpret the phrase 'in Israel' to mean within Israel, but among the nations of the world one comparable did arise—namely Balaam. Ba'al HaTurim cites a received reading that this prophet 'arose for a time,' meaning the prophecy was momentary rather than continuous. Jeremiah 38:17–20 records Jeremiah's counsel to Zedekiah to surrender to the officers of the king of Babylon, which Zedekiah refused, leading to his exile. Moses' acceptance of Jethro's counsel in Exodus 18:24 is met with the reward of平安 coming to one's place.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 34:10" "Jeremiah 38:17–20" "Exodus 18:24"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["איעצך" "לכה איעצך" "וכי איעצך לא תשמע אלי"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "איעצך", :refs ["Exodus 18:19" "Numbers 24:14" "1 Kings 1:12" "Jeremiah 38:15"], :n 4, :lens :exact} {:phrase "לכה איעצך", :refs ["Numbers 24:14"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "וכי איעצך לא תשמע אלי", :refs ["Jeremiah 38:15"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "Gezerah shavah: the shared rare word איעצך links Balaam's prophecy to Moses' prophecy.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Contrast: Moses heeded advice and stayed in his place; Zedekiah ignored advice and was exiled from his place.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:17:24.555143752Z", :model "glm-5.2"}